I am sure you can find one of your own guards in your own stronghold.	在自己的要塞裡，你想必找得到自己的衛兵。
He is where a Treasurer usually is. In the Treasury.	他就在司庫平常所在之處——寶庫裡。
Worship of the Christ god arose in the Far East about 700 years ago and has spread west ever since. To some he is a prophet, to others the son of God. He preached much of love, of compassion, and forgiveness for the sins of others.	基督信仰約在七百年前興起於遠東，自此便向西方傳播不絕。在某些人眼中，他是先知；在另一些人眼中，他是神之子。他傳揚愛、憐憫，以及寬恕他人罪愆的教誨。
Mithras is a warrior-god which only men are allowed to worship and in great secret. He was most popular among the Roman soldiers who brought this worship with them to our island centuries ago.	米夏拉是一位戰神，只有男子才被允許崇拜他，而且須極為隱密。此信仰在羅馬士兵之間最為盛行，數世紀前由他們帶到我們這座島上。
Glastonbury Tor has been a sacred hill for centuries. The legend of Joseph of Arimathea claims the Grail is hidden there.	格列斯登伯利山數世紀以來一直是座聖山。亞利馬太的約瑟的傳說宣稱，聖杯就藏於此處。
It is a body of water to the north where currently the Lady of the Lake dwells.	那是北方的一片水域，湖中女神如今便棲居於此。
It is your major port in the south where you must go to take the ship to other lands.	那是你南方的主要港口，你須經此搭船前往他方國度。
This dark and dangerous forest borders Glastonbury Tor and you must pass through it to reach the sacred hill.	這座陰暗而危險的森林與格列斯登伯利山相鄰，你必須穿越此處才能抵達那座聖山。
If you wish to know more about that place, study the map, and I shall instruct you.	你若想多了解那個地方，仔細研究地圖，我便會指引你。
Let us leave discussion of that for another time.	此事容後再議。
I know you would not be so rude.	我知道你不會如此無禮。
Say rather godspeed, for I shall be with you in spirit-voice throughout your mission.	不如說「一路順風」吧，因為在你此行途中，我將以心神之聲與你同在。
Aye, may the god you worship speed you to your destiny, Arthur.	正是，願你所信奉的神明，助你抵達命運所在，亞瑟。
Use your eyes, Arthur, it's already closed.	睜大你的眼睛，亞瑟，它已經關上了。
You have taken the only thing I wish you to have.	我要你擁有的東西，你已經拿到了。
Use your eyes, Arthur.  It IS open.	睜大你的眼睛，亞瑟，它確實開著。
Hmmm....it is around here somewhere. I simply cannot remember where I put it.	唔……應該就在附近某處。我實在想不起放到哪去了。
It is attached to my wall.	它就掛在我的牆上。
King you may be, but do not lay hands upon that which belongs to Merlin the enchanter.	你或許貴為王者，但休想染指屬於魔法師梅林之物。
The lodestone is the only object in this room which you may take. The rest belongs to Merlin the Enchanter and you are not to lay hands upon them.	指北針是這房裡唯一你可以拿走的東西。其餘皆屬魔法師梅林所有，你不得染指。
But....you must excuse an old man. I have forgotten where I put the lodestone. It is around here somewhere.	但……你得原諒一個老人。我忘了把指北針放到哪去了，應該就在附近某處。
Search if you like, but DO NOT TOUCH ANYTHING ELSE!	你要找便找，但除此之外什麼都不准碰！
By the Red Dragon, I will not warn you again! Do not lay hands upon anything that is not meant for you.	以紅龍之名起誓，我不會再警告你第二次！不屬於你的東西，休得伸手。
You were thinking of spending the rest of your life as a toad, perhaps?	你該不會是想餘生都當隻蟾蜍度過吧？
My darling boy, I did not know you cared.	我親愛的孩子，我不知道你竟如此在乎我。
I never kiss men with beards.	我從不親吻蓄鬍的男子。
What a completely ridiculous notion.	這想法簡直荒唐至極。
I enjoy the mingling of scents: the fumes of alchemy, the herbs drying upon my wall, burning candles, even the musty odor of the old scroll I am studying.	我喜愛這些氣味交融：煉金的煙氣、牆上風乾的藥草、燃燒的蠟燭，甚至我正在研讀的那卷古老卷軸散發的霉味。
Ah, the symbol of love.	啊，愛的象徵。
You had best keep it.	你最好留著它。
Now why would you want to give me something that I have given you?	你為何要把我送你的東西，又送還給我？
You have greater need of it than I.	你比我更需要它。
A most gracious gesture, but I have no need of it.	此舉甚是慷慨，但我並不需要它。
If I am ever in need of help, rest assured you will be the first to know.	若我有朝一日需要幫助，放心，你必是第一個知曉的人。
You do not have your sword.	你並未佩劍。
There will be time enough for that later and I am not fond of cold steel in my presence.	此事來日方長，況且我不喜冷鐵近身。
Truly, I think your hearing is impaired. Have I not warned you against this once?	說真的，我看你耳朵是出了毛病。我不是警告過你一次了嗎？
I am your mentor and advisor, but I will not tolerate being threatened in this fashion.	我是你的導師與謀士，但我不會容忍被如此威脅。
Inside my chest is a lodestone, a magical stone that will always show you where true north lies.  This one is shaped like a tiny sword, the tip of which will point to north as it dangles from a string attached to its center.	我箱子裡有一枚指北針，一種能指出正北方向的魔法石。這一枚打造成小劍形狀，以繩繫在中心懸垂，劍尖便會指向北方。
Take it, Arthur.   I prepared it especially for you.	拿去吧，亞瑟。這是我特地為你準備的。
It is a map of the Summer Lands, as your kingdom is often known;	這是夏地的地圖——你的王國常被如此稱呼；
Cornwall to the west, and some lands beyond, including the island of Eire.	西邊是康瓦爾，再往外還有一些土地，包括愛爾蘭島。
However, you should study it very closely before you leave and determine where your search for the Grail should take you.	然而，你在啟程前應仔細研究此圖，判斷你尋找聖杯之路該往何處去。
Since you cannot keep your hands to yourself, you can do without them for awhile.	既然你管不住自己的手，那就讓你暫時沒有手可用。
When you apologize, I will consider returning you to your native form.	待你道歉之後，我會考慮讓你恢復原形。
It would seem you refuse to learn a lesson.  Be gone from my sight.	看來你是不肯記取教訓。從我眼前消失。
Your stubbornness defies belief. I will waste no more time upon you, fool of a king.	你的頑固簡直令人難以置信。我不會再在你身上浪費時間了，愚昧的王啊。
PRESS F6 TO EXIT	按 F6 離開
Use arrows to move, or select with mouse.	使用方向鍵移動，或用滑鼠點選。
You see the Summer Lands, as your kingdom is often known, with Cornwall to the west and river Thames coming from the east.	你看見夏地——你的王國常被如此稱呼，西邊是康瓦爾，泰晤士河則從東邊流入。
Take careful note of the locations that may be of import to your search. This will prevent you from wasting much time later.	仔細留意那些可能對你的尋覓有重要意義的地點，這能省下你日後不少時間。
Do I really need to tell you that this is the rack upon which your mail tunic was hung?	我真有必要告訴你，這是掛你鎖子甲的架子嗎？
Your mail tunic is made of overlapping metal scales, a design copied from Roman cavalry armour.	你的鎖子甲是以層疊的金屬鱗片製成，這設計仿自羅馬騎兵的鎧甲。
Upon this shield is the Red Dragon, in token of your surname, Pendragon, which comes from the Welsh words meaning "supreme war chief".	這面盾牌上繪著紅龍，象徵你的姓氏「潘德拉貢」，此名源自威爾斯語，意為「至高的戰爭統帥」。
You received your sword, Excaliber, from the Lady in the Lake.  By Her Blessings, may it serve you well.	你的劍——聖劍，得自湖中女神。願蒙她的祝福，這把劍將不負所用。
Your purse remains where you last put it, upon your table.	你的錢囊仍在你上次放置之處——你的桌上。
When you are in need of solitude, this is your room.  It is sparsely furnished, as befits a warrior-king.	當你需要獨處時，這便是你的房間。陳設簡樸，正合戰士之王的身分。
They are made of the same grey stone as the rest of Camelot.	它們與肯萊特其餘部分一樣，皆以灰石砌成。
There are two stands in your room. One holds your mail tunic. In the other corner is the rack holding your clothes.	你房裡有兩座衣架。一座掛著你的鎖子甲，另一角的架子則掛著你的衣物。
The Celts, like many others, worshipped a Triple Goddess in her three forms: virgin, mother, and crone, which in turn represent creation, life and death.	凱爾特人和許多其他民族一樣，崇拜以三種樣貌顯現的三重女神：處女、母親與老嫗，分別象徵創造、生命與死亡。
From these windows you see the outer wall of Camelot and the hills, fields and forest beyond.	從這些窗戶望出去，你能見到肯萊特的外牆，以及牆外的丘陵、田野與森林。
Unfortunately, you cannot see the Queen's bower from here.  Rumour in the palace has it that she placed her bower deliberately out of your sight.  But that is only rumour.	可惜從這裡看不見王后的閨閣。宮中流言說，她是刻意把閨閣安置在你視線之外。但那終究只是流言。
Aye, they are nice trees. Now, kindly get your mind on your mission.	是啊，那些樹確實不錯。現在，請將心思放回你的使命上。
It is a heavy wood and metal door.	這是一扇沉重的木製鐵門。
Your court clothes hang upon the stand in the corner.	你的朝服掛在牆角的衣架上。
A sturdy set of travelling clothes hangs upon a wooden stand in the south corner of your room. Another stand against the northeastern wall holds your tunic and armour.	一套堅韌的行裝掛在你房間南角的木架上。東北牆邊另有一座衣架，掛著你的鎖子甲與鎧甲。
Aye, the lack of helmet is a serious oversight, m'lord.   You will have to compensate with extra caution.  You must keep your head if you are to keep your head.	正是，缺了頭盔確實是一大疏漏，吾王。你得加倍謹慎以為彌補。你得保持頭腦冷靜，才能保住你的項上人頭。
Your bedspread was lovingly made by your wife.	你的床罩，是你的妻子悉心縫製而成。
Alas, the queen is not here now.	可惜，王后此刻不在這裡。
You cannot see it from here.	從這裡看不見它。
You should have a word with your servant. A great deal of dust has been swept under this rug.	你該找僕人談談了，這地毯底下掃進了不少灰塵。
Aside from stirring up the dust, this will not accomplish much.	除了揚起灰塵之外，這樣做不會有什麼用處。
There is clearly nothing under the table.	桌子底下顯然什麼都沒有。
Gwen is in the bower, not here.	昆海兒在閨閣裡，不在這裡。
It is a bed, of course.  Even a King must sometimes sleep alone when the Queen is indisposed.	這當然是張床。即便貴為國王，王后偶有不適時，也得獨自安眠。
Your purse lies where you tossed it upon the table last night.	你的錢囊，就躺在你昨晚隨手扔在桌上的地方。
It is a sturdy, oak table.	這是一張堅固的橡木桌。
Closet? Sounds like the French word "clos", but there is no enclosure in this room.	衣櫃？聽起來像法文的「clos」，但這房裡並沒有這樣的隔間。
A three-armed Celtic symbol adorns your rug, perhaps a reminder of the three-fold Great Goddess of creation, life and death.	你的地毯上飾有一個三臂凱爾特符號，或許是在提醒創造、生命與死亡的三重大女神。
There are two symbols here. One is upon your shield, the other upon your rug.	這裡有兩個符號，一個在你的盾牌上，另一個在你的地毯上。
The red dragon upon your shield is your symbol. You are Arthur Pendragon.	盾牌上的紅龍是你的象徵。你是亞瑟·潘德拉貢。
Preparation is vital.  Body, heart, mind, and spirit must all be in readiness before you leave Camelot.	準備至關重要。在離開肯萊特之前，身、心、意、靈皆須齊備。
Just walk through it.	直接穿過去便是。
It is a heavy door which swings shut by its own weight.	這是一扇沉重的門，會因自身重量而自行關上。
The floor beneath it is the same as the rest of your floor.	它底下的地板，與房裡其餘地板並無不同。
This is no time for a nap.  Your mission is urgent and every second you delay, your people suffer.	現在不是小憩的時候。你的使命刻不容緩，每耽擱一秒，你的子民便多受一分苦。
What an incredibly foolish notion.	這想法真是愚蠢至極。
That would get you nowhere fast.	那樣做只會讓你原地打轉。
It is quite satisfied being where it is.	它待在原處便挺自在的。
A token from Gwenhyver is better kept close to your heart.	昆海兒所贈的信物，最好貼身珍藏。
They are not sturdy enough for your mission. Leave them here.	它們不夠堅韌，無法應付你的使命，留在這裡吧。
You are already wearing them.	你已經穿在身上了。
You are wearing your armour...as if I should need to tell you that.	你已經穿著鎧甲了……這種事還用我來提醒嗎。
Why?	為什麼？
I sincerely hope you have made up your mind this time.	我誠心希望你這回已經拿定主意了。
Your servants are already preparing a pack for your journey.  It will surely contain a sturdier blanket than this.	你的僕從已在為你此行備妥行囊，裡頭想必會有一條比這條更堅實的毯子。
A bit large to carry about, one would think.	想來這東西帶著走未免太過龐大。
It would only get in the way.	那只會礙手礙腳。
It's not here.	它不在這裡。
Your shield is upon your arm.	你的盾牌已戴在臂上。
A shield gets in the way of putting on other armour. You need to get your mail tunic and sword first.	盾牌會妨礙你穿戴其他鎧甲。你得先穿上鎖子甲、佩好劍才行。
Your sword is strapped at your side.	你的劍已繫在腰間。
Before you can strap on your sword, you need to be wearing your mail tunic.	在佩劍之前，你得先穿上鎖子甲。
You are already wearing your armor.	你已經穿著鎧甲了。
You cannot wear armour over your court clothes. Your travelling clothes are in the south corner of your room.	你不能把鎧甲套在朝服外頭。你的行裝就在房間南角。
They would not do for this trip. Leave them here.	這趟旅程用不上它們，留在這裡吧。
You already are wearing them.	你已經穿在身上了。
That is not a very good reason.	這理由可不怎麼站得住腳。
How wise of you.	你可真是明智。
Hmmph.  That was truly pointless.	哼，那真是白費工夫。
I am certain that if you talk to your Treasurer or question him correctly, you will learn all you need.	我確信，只要你去找司庫問個明白，便能得知你所需的一切。
Remember, 25 copper coins equals 5 silver coins and 5 silver coins equals one gold coin.	記住，二十五枚銅幣等於五枚銀幣，五枚銀幣等於一枚金幣。
It is made of heavy oak planks, with a trapdoor for the only entrance.	此處以厚重橡木板築成，唯一的入口是一道活板門。
This tower stronghold was built to protect your store of coins and other valuables. The bundles on the right are new, however.	這座塔樓要塞建來守護你的錢幣與其他財物。不過，右邊那幾捆包裹是新添的。
They are made of the same grey stone as the rest of Camelot.  Only thicker.	它們與肯萊特其餘部分一樣，皆以灰石砌成，只是更為厚實。
You cannot see much of it from this tower stronghold.	從這座塔樓要塞裡，你看不太到外頭的景象。
The trap door is heavy and easily defended.	這道活板門十分沉重，易守難攻。
Aye, 'tis a torch.	正是，這是一支火把。
The huge jars contain your entire wealth of gold, silver and copper coins. The chests contain other forms of wealth. I do not know what is in the bundles.	這幾口大甕裝著你全部的金、銀、銅幣財富。箱子裡則是其他形式的財物。至於包裹裡是什麼，我就不得而知了。
The pillars of this tower are quite strong and thick.	這座塔樓的柱子相當堅固粗實。
They are bundles that are stored here.	那些是存放在此處的包裹。
They lead down to the main floor of Camelot.	它們通往肯萊特的主樓層。
The chests contain gems and jewels set in gold and silver, plates and goblets of gold and silver and other such fine items.	箱子裡裝著鑲嵌於金銀之中的寶石與珠玉、金銀打造的盤碟與高腳杯，以及其他諸如此類的珍品。
He is a powerfully built man, well able to defend this tower and your treasure. Heed his advice.	他體格強健，足以守衛這座塔樓與你的財寶。你該聽從他的建言。
There is gold in the jar on the right.	右邊的甕裡裝著金幣。
There is silver in the middle jar.	中間的甕裡裝著銀幣。
There is copper in the leftmost jar.	最左邊的甕裡裝著銅幣。
The three large jars contain gold, silver, and copper coins.	這三口大甕裝著金幣、銀幣與銅幣。
Your treasurer has a huge sword and knows how to use it.	你的司庫佩著一把巨劍，而且深諳用劍之道。
In this enclosed room, the odor of a sweaty man, oily torch, and cold metal is most concentrated.	在這密閉的房間裡，汗味、油煙火把味與冷硬金屬味格外濃重。
